{
  "title": "About Table API Keys",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "410a4248d5faf888",
      "text": "The Table plugin allows writes from remote computers provided they include a header with a valid API key — the same arrangement as the [[JSON Plugin]] it was cloned from. Here we describe how a server administrator can manage keys."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1da4163caa47ecff",
      "text": "Valid keys are kept in a tokens.json file, one file for each site hosted by the server. If server data is kept in the customary ~/.wiki directory, look to these locations."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "b7f07a774118424b",
      "text": "~/.wiki/status/plugin/table/tokens.json\n~/.wiki/<site>/status/plugin/table/tokens.json"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "176d2730d7aa8892",
      "text": "The tokens are listed by slug, where * means all slugs."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "3003eee43f1a8edd",
      "text": "tokens = {slug: keys}\nkeys = {key: info}\ninfo = {id: string, nb: string}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "70a961b4e24ba01c",
      "text": "A complete tokens.json file might look like this."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "91f4b5df79e69f15",
      "text": "{\n  \"table-plugin\": {\n    \"429c7b\": {\n      \"id\": \"demo\",\n      \"nb\": \"widely known, discard if abused\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"*\": {\n    \"79ce4a\": {\n      \"id\": \"wildcard\",\n      \"nb\": \"experimental use only\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "972c916542823900",
      "text": "The info fields are for the convenience of administrators. The id is recorded on the item as the writer; the nb field stays private. Longer keys are encouraged. The file is read once when the server starts, so restart after editing it."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "00227dc75a98cf4a",
      "text": "Writers signed in as the site owner on a private farm do not need a key: the [[Farm Plugin]] mounts POST /system/api/table/write.json behind the wiki's own login instead."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "a89436afba3a4a4d",
      "text": "# See\n\n- [[About Table Plugin]]\n- [[About JSON API Keys]]"
    }
  ],
